Luke Franks

Part 1: what do you observe from the printf, printf & fflush, write?

USING WRITE
luke@Lukes-MacBook-Air-87 Lab0 % ./who_runs_first | sort | uniq -c        
 996 childparent
   4 parentchild

USING printf and fflush
luke@Lukes-MacBook-Air-87 Lab0 % ./who_runs_first | sort | uniq -c        
 991 childparent
   9 parentchild

When just using printf, parents kept executing before the child and everything was
not being scheduled right.

When the program is slept for 1 second, everything executes correctly. It just takes
a long time.